      "message": "How? I\u0027ve been trying to come up with a way to do that (and actually just DM\u0027d you before seeing this comment). I can do that in the header, sure, but the OS only has the single unmangled symbol. I haven\u0027t come up with a useful way to preserve the reference-based API yet. Symbol versioning is almost what I want, but without a way to backport the new version that\u0027s not useful.\n\nI suppose I could add the reference-based one as an inline for C++. It\u0027d preserve source-compat. That\u0027s maybe worth it in its own right, but this change would scare me a lot less if there were a way to preserve the reference-using definition in the OS.",
